7203	{"artifactId":"LLD-aef82b034d7209fa-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-aef82b034d7209fa-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:21:59.624Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Batching the five model-backed dimensions and bypassing structured retries for size refusals addresses the stated root cause.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies whole-grounding calls and repeated size refusals. The five prompt builders serialize grounding.symbols wholesale; their judges call completeStructured through withStructuredRetry. That helper catches non-AbortError failures and continues to the next attempt. [files: docs/standalone/review-every-changed-symbol-story-too-E20261018aef82b03/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/conventions.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/quality.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"Retain both the dimension batching and the refusal-specific retry bypass.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified MAP cross product and note-key REDUCE adjudicate every obligation even when there are no symbols.","evidence":"prepareCoverageGrounding explicitly returns 'if (groundingMode === \u000027degraded\u000027) return { symbols: [] };'. buildCoveragePrompt then instructs 'Judge ONLY the promised tests against the test-record results'. The proposed MAP operates on symbol parts × context parts and REDUCE groups emitted notes; with zero symbol parts, neither supplies an adjudication for promised tests. The same problem affects obligations receiving no notes. No initialization of obligation keys or context-only calls is specified. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, docs/standalone/review-every-changed-symbol-story-too-E20261018aef82b03/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Initialize adjudication keys from every clause, FR and promised test independently of MAP output. Define context-only calls for empty symbol sets and explicitly adjudicate keys with zero evidence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The controller currently emits all dimension prompts and the whole grounding in one frame, while CLI size errors reach the generic retry path.","evidence":"emitJudgementsResult returns 'next: \u000027emit_judgements\u000027', prompts, schema, grounding and state together. runCodex throws a plain Error for error/turn.failed events; completeStructuredOnce throws a plain Error for Claude is_error envelopes. withStructuredRetry treats these thrown errors as validation failures. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"Preserve the legacy frame for fitting reviews and intercept size errors before both retry classifiers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The identified judge, runner, controller state/type and MCP registration sites cover the principal execution and persistence boundaries for the new job protocol.","evidence":"runner.ts registers all five model-backed judges and persists their DimensionResults. The controller injects supplied dimension results into that same runner. Its types define the judgements input and emit_judgements output; state-store.ts retains the payload behind opaque tokens. The MCP registration forwards 'forward(\u000027insrc_code_review_step\u000027, rawArgs, extra)' unchanged, so adding answers to its schema is necessary and correctly identified. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/types.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/state-store.ts, src/mcp/server.ts]","action":"Make legacy judgements optional in the controller input type when answers is supplied, and preserve parts when constructing final dimension results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Serial judging, failure before persistence, and path-specific out-of-scope handling are existing invariants that the proposed job integration can preserve.","evidence":"runCodeReview awaits each slot.judge in a for-of loop and reaches record writes only after all judges and validation succeed. Daemon judges filter findings against changedFiles. Controller validateJudgements instead retains dropped findings as outOfScope, and driveRunner reports scopeDropped without counting those findings. The design explicitly preserves these boundaries. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Apply these policies after job aggregation; retain controller outOfScope metadata and normalize coverage once against the complete prepared grounding.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance tests establish complete obligation coverage for every supported grounding mode.","evidence":"The proposed tests exercise evidence distributed across parts and oversized records, but none explicitly combines an over-budget record or contract with zero symbols, or requires an obligation with zero emitted notes to be adjudicated. Existing coverage tests include empty grounding, but use a fake provider that returns a scripted answer regardless of its prompt. Those tests cannot detect the missing MAP/REDUCE work described above. [files: docs/standalone/review-every-changed-symbol-story-too-E20261018aef82b03/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/coverage.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts]","action":"Add prompt-sensitive daemon and controller tests with empty prepared grounding, an oversized record, and both passing and missing promised tests. Also test clauses and FRs receiving no MAP notes. Assert that every obligation reaches adjudication and missing obligations produce findings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-18T19:21:59.624Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
